# TajStay MASTER SPEC (binding)

One brand · four shells: **Public Desktop** · **Consumer Mobile/PWA** · **Owner CRM** · **Admin CRM**. Shared design system; different IA.

## Hard stops

- No one-shot rewrite of the whole app. After each authorized BLOCK: report CODE/TEST/DEPLOYED/REAL RUNTIME/EVIDENCE, then **STOP**.
- No production DB wipe / destructive prod probes without explicit permission.
- Frontend ≠ AuthZ. Backend must enforce.
- No mint/light text on white; no website footer under mobile app/workspace nav; no Consumer tabs in Admin/Owner; no raw enums in Admin UI; no blank white panels; no fake AI.
- Canonical brand: **TajStay**.

## Visual direction (foundation later)

Light canvas + deep green brand (`~#0F7A4D`) + restrained gold. Semantic tokens only. Sans for app/CRM; serif only marketing display.

## Security priority (before redesign)

1. **P0-S1** — remove secret-word primitive; harden owner recovery; fail-close insecure credentials; Admin Audit foundation.
2. **P0-S2** — AuthZ / destructive ops / RBAC prep.
3. **P0-R1** — 500 traces + blank panel root cause.
4. Then Design System → Layout shells → screen blocks.

## Current authorized work

Only the BLOCK named in the latest user message. Default if unclear: finish in-progress P0 security remediation and stop — do **not** start Design System / Consumer redesign.

## Acceptance

`PASS` requires evidence beyond grep/build. Statuses: PASS | FAIL | BLOCKED | UNKNOWN.

Every visual/runtime claim must cite **deployment URL + exact commit SHA** (production `tajstay.site` ≠ Vercel preview — never mix as one baseline).

## DESKTOP VISUAL BASELINE (screenshot review — evidence only)

Do **not** redesign these screens until P0-S1+ security blocks are closed and Design System Foundation is authorized.

1. **Vercel preview Home** — good **structural** baseline: keep hero hierarchy, desktop header concept, search composition; migrate Public Desktop from full-green canvas to light premium (green as accent/CTA/panel, not whole page).
2. **Profile + Security desktop** — nearest existing **visual** reference for light surfaces, readable dark text, border density, calm green accents. Prefer this over green Admin for DS work later.
3. **Admin desktop today** — **not** a visual target. Separate light CRM shell; remove public nav (`Главная / Поиск / О сервисе`) and consumer hotel assistant from Admin/Owner.
4. **Admin Sidebar IA** — largely keep (Обзор / Люди / Отели / Контент / Финансы / Операции); later add Audit Log / analytics. Restyle to light sidebar + semantic active states.
5. **Legacy delete (dependency audit first, do not redesign):** AI Concierge, «Случайный бюджет», fake/random recommendation UI/handlers/API/tests.
6. **Popular hotels:** no one-card + empty vast desktop void — featured layout or responsive 3–4 card grid by count.
7. Real hotel photos over TajStay-logo placeholders; empty photo = neutral «Фото пока не добавлено».
8. Brand spelling **TajStay** only (not Tajstay in CMS banners).
9. Trust («Почему нам доверяют») — keep idea, light presentation, no absolute unverified claims.
10. Footer — OK structural base; deep green OK as single large dark band at bottom of Public Website only.
11. Desktop search: prefer one-row booking bar on large desktop; two-row OK mid-desktop.
12. Shell leak proof: PublicShell ≠ AdminShell ≠ OwnerShell ≠ ConsumerAccountShell.

### Scores (baseline, not acceptance)

Public Home structure ~7 · Public visual ~5 · Profile/Security ~7.5 · Old home/AI sections ~4 · Admin desktop ~3.5

After security: Design System Foundation uses Profile/Security light logic as first visual reference — not current green Admin.

## MOBILE WHITE/GREEN RUNTIME REFERENCE (screenshot review — evidence only)

New mobile runtime screenshots confirm the final TajStay color composition. **Do not** treat this as authorization to redesign every screen yet — use as direction evidence after P0 security / when Design System Foundation is authorized. Prefer **systemic semantic tokens**, not page-by-page CSS.

**Composition formula (project-wide):**

```text
background = white / near-white
functional identity = deep green blocks, CTAs, selected states, icons
content cards = white / light
premium accents = controlled gold (Owner/role), not whole Owner CRM
CRM analytics = green / amber / blue / red by meaning (allowed)
```

Search pattern (Home / Search) — keep as principle:

```text
WHITE BACKGROUND
  → large DEEP-GREEN search component
  → LIGHT inputs inside (not same dark green as panel — placeholders must remain readable)
  → bright green Search CTA
WHITE BACKGROUND
```

**Keep as reference:**

- White main page background (Tours, History, Search, Profile, Admin Users, Admin Dashboard).
- Large green functional / search blocks.
- White/light content cards; green primary buttons; green icons / selected states.
- Controlled semantic analytics colors; gold Owner/Premium accents.
- Light Admin/CRM workspace (white KPI cards, green borders, light bottom nav + green active).
- Mobile Profile structure (white page/cards, green icons, light-green info cards, dark text, role, verification) — polish details, no radical rewrite.
- Tours category cards may stay deep green; fix **foreground** (title/icon → white or light on brand).
- History support card may stay green functional card; main text white + bright link/CTA.
- Consumer deep-green bottom nav is allowed **if** inactive labels/icons have sufficient light contrast; active = bright TajStay green; selected bg slightly lighter than bar.
- Admin/Owner: white/light bottom/sidebar preferred; active = TajStay Green (Consumer and CRM nav backgrounds need not match).

**Do not keep as reference:**

- Low-contrast gray/mint text on deep green.
- White/mint text on white (Admin KPI leftovers).
- Duplicate second TajStay logo in Consumer header right (prefer notification / user avatar / action / nothing; Admin hamburger OK).
- Oversized assistant speech bubble always visible; prefer small branded FAB → bottom sheet «Помощник TajStay».
- Hotel-card TajStay-logo placeholders instead of real photos; empty → «Фото пока не добавлено».
- Clipped History horizontal tabs (scroll+snap, compact chips, or collapsed filters).
- Narrow half-width hotel result card on mobile (near full viewport width).
- Consumer marketing footer / © inside mobile app chrome.
- Inline Admin role dropdown + blocking checkbox as final UX (detail → confirm + reason + audit later).
- Near-black unexplained floating chrome that fights white-green-gold system.

**Provenance note (code, not guess):** Consumer right-header “second logo” risk = `BrandMark` (left) + `HeaderMobileActions` → `ProfileAvatar` (right when logged in) — avatar must not be the brand mark. Near-black mobile float + speech nudge = product `TstAssistant` (`.tst-assistant__fab` + `.tst-assistant__hint`), not Admin/Owner (FAB hidden on CRM shells). If a third black circle appears only in some browsers/tools, exclude from TajStay chrome.

Do **not** copy current CSS hex values from screenshots. Screenshots = visual direction evidence only (always cite deployment URL + commit SHA when claiming runtime).
